EXECUTION-ONLY MODE. NO PLANNING. Edit files via Edit tool. Production-grade.

Repo: `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/InkOS`

## Sprint 17 Track A — Tax mirror path on `payment_intent.succeeded` + per-tax-line commission split

S16 left a documented gap: `tax_amount_cents` was set to 0 at PaymentIntent create time and never updated via webhook. S17 closes the gap and adds per-tax-line commission split attribution.

## Context (load first)

- File to extend: `lib/payments/process-stripe-event.ts` — Track D from S16 added SAGA confirmation. Now extend the same `payment_intent.succeeded` handler.
- Plan: `~/.claude/plans/so-this-is-whole-parallel-pillow.md` — S17 EPIC 1 row 17
- Lessons: `~/.claude/memory/projects/inkos-lessons.md` — load Tier 1 + S13/S14/S15/S16 appendices (CC1-CC30)
- Source of truth: `lib/payments/contracts.ts` — JUST ADDED:
  - `RPC.COMMISSION_SPLIT_TAX_LINE_RECORD` — `CommissionSplitTaxLineRecordArgs` / `Result`
  - Extended `CommissionSplitRecordArgs` with optional `taxAmountCents`, `taxLineId`, `jurisdiction` (Track D ships SQL function update)
- Existing: `RPC.STRIPE_CHARGE_UPDATE_STATUS_FROM_WEBHOOK` (S13) — extend args to include tax_amount_cents (Track D updates SQL)
- Existing: `RPC.TAX_REMITTANCE_ACCRUE` (S13) — accrue per-jurisdiction tax for quarterly remittance

## Hard rules

1. NO `any`. Strict TS.
2. NO Stripe API calls inside webhook handler (CC: hot path forbidden). Use only data in `event.data.object`.
3. Webhook idempotent — replay safe via webhook_event_insert (CC7).
4. RPC constants only. No inline strings.
5. Service-role client (passed in by caller).
6. Pino logger. No console.log.
7. Money in cents (`bigint` DB / `CentsAmount` TS).
8. Use structural type pattern (`StripePaymentIntentShape`, `StripeChargeShape`) — workers can't transitively import `next/*` (CC12).
9. `supabase.from.bind(supabase)` for any cast pattern (CC28).

## Stripe payload shape — what's available in webhook

`event.data.object` for `payment_intent.succeeded` contains:
- `id` — pi_xxx
- `amount` — total charged (includes tax)
- `currency`
- `latest_charge` — string charge id OR null
- `metadata` — our inkos_* fields
- `automatic_tax: { enabled: boolean, status: 'requires_location_inputs'|'failed'|'complete', liability: 'application'|'self' }`
- `amount_details` — Stripe wraps tax amount here in newer API versions: `{ tax: { amount: number } }` (NOT always present; check existence)

If `amount_details.tax` is present → use it.
If not → fall back to: `tax_amount_cents = pi.amount - (charge.amount_subtotal || base+tip)`. For S17, simpler heuristic: use `amount_details.tax.amount` if present, else 0 (log info: "tax not in PI payload — webhook tax mirror skipped, will need cron sync").

For per-tax-line breakdown: `amount_details.tax_breakdown` (Stripe May 2024+) is an array `[{ amount: number, jurisdiction: { country, state? }, ... }]`. NOT all API versions populate this. If absent, fall back to single-line accrual using studio's primary location jurisdiction.

## What to add to `lib/payments/process-stripe-event.ts`

Extend `StripePaymentIntentShape` with optional fields:

```ts
interface StripePaymentIntentShape {
  id: string;
  latest_charge?: string | { id: string } | null;
  metadata?: Record<string, string | undefined> | null;
  amount?: number;                                    // S17
  currency?: string | null;                           // S17
  amount_details?: {                                   // S17
    tax?: { amount: number } | null;
    tax_breakdown?: Array<{
      amount: number;
      jurisdiction?: { country?: string; state?: string | null } | null;
      tax_rate_details?: { tax_type?: string | null } | null;
    }> | null;
  } | null;
}
```

In `handlePaymentIntentStatusChange` for `eventType === 'payment_intent.succeeded'`, AFTER the existing `confirm_deposit_application` + `commission_split_record` block, add:

```ts
// === S17 — Tax mirror + per-tax-line attribution ===

const taxTotal = pi.amount_details?.tax?.amount ?? 0;
const taxBreakdown = pi.amount_details?.tax_breakdown ?? [];

// 1. Update stripe_charges.tax_amount_cents via charge update RPC.
// (Track D extends stripe_charge_update_status_from_webhook to accept p_tax_amount_cents.)
// We pass tax even if 0 — explicit update.
const { error: chargeTaxErr } = await supabase.rpc(RPC.STRIPE_CHARGE_UPDATE_STATUS_FROM_WEBHOOK, {
  p_payment_intent_id: pi.id,
  p_status: 'succeeded',
  p_charge_id: typeof pi.latest_charge === 'string' ? pi.latest_charge : pi.latest_charge?.id ?? null,
  p_transfer_id: null,                                  // Stripe doesn't expose transfer_id on PI
  p_application_fee_id: null,
  p_tax_amount_cents: taxTotal,                         // S17: actual tax now
});
if (chargeTaxErr) {
  logger.error({ pi_id: pi.id, err: chargeTaxErr },
    'S17: stripe_charge_update_status_from_webhook (tax pass) failed');
  throw chargeTaxErr;
}

// 2. Per-tax-line attribution to commission_splits.
// We need the parent split id — re-query the split we just inserted.
if (taxBreakdown.length > 0 && studioId && bookingId) {
  // Find the parent split (the one we just inserted in the prior block).
  const fromUntyped = supabase.from.bind(supabase) as unknown as (table: string) => {
    select: (cols: string) => {
      eq: (col: string, val: string) => {
        eq: (col2: string, val2: string) => {
          order: (col: string, opts: { ascending: boolean }) => {
            limit: (n: number) => {
              maybeSingle: () => Promise<{ data: { id: string } | null; error: unknown }>;
            };
          };
        };
      };
    };
  };
  const { data: parentSplitData } = await fromUntyped('commission_splits')
    .select('id')
    .eq('booking_id', bookingId)
    .eq('kind', 'split')
    .order('created_at', { ascending: false })
    .limit(1)
    .maybeSingle();

  if (parentSplitData) {
    const parentSplitId = parentSplitData.id;

    for (const line of taxBreakdown) {
      const country = line.jurisdiction?.country ?? null;
      const state = line.jurisdiction?.state ?? null;
      const jurisdiction = state ? `${country ?? 'US'}-${state}` : (country ?? 'UNKNOWN');
      // Synthetic tax_line_id — Stripe tax_breakdown items don't have stable IDs across replays;
      // we hash (parent_split, jurisdiction) to make replay idempotent.
      const taxLineId = `${parentSplitId}:${jurisdiction}`;

      const { error: lineErr } = await supabase.rpc(RPC.COMMISSION_SPLIT_TAX_LINE_RECORD, {
        p_parent_split_id: parentSplitId,
        p_tax_line_id: taxLineId,
        p_jurisdiction: jurisdiction,
        p_tax_amount_cents: line.amount,
      });
      if (lineErr) {
        logger.error({ pi_id: pi.id, parent_split: parentSplitId, jurisdiction, err: lineErr },
          'S17: commission_split_tax_line_record failed — recoverable via reconciliation');
      }

      // 3. Accrue to tax_remittance_ledger per jurisdiction.
      // Studio's primary location_id needs to be looked up — reuse the studio metadata.
      // For S17 simplicity: derive period as YYYY-Qn from the event timestamp.
      const eventDate = new Date();
      const quarter = Math.floor(eventDate.getMonth() / 3) + 1;
      const period = `${eventDate.getFullYear()}-Q${quarter}`;

      // Resolve studio's primary location_id.
      const fromUntypedSelect = supabase.from.bind(supabase) as unknown as (table: string) => {
        select: (cols: string) => {
          eq: (col: string, val: string) => {
            limit: (n: number) => {
              maybeSingle: () => Promise<{ data: { id: string } | null; error: unknown }>;
            };
          };
        };
      };
      const { data: locationData } = await fromUntypedSelect('locations')
        .select('id')
        .eq('studio_id', studioId)
        .limit(1)
        .maybeSingle();

      if (locationData) {
        const { error: accrueErr } = await supabase.rpc(RPC.TAX_REMITTANCE_ACCRUE, {
          p_studio_id: studioId,
          p_location_id: locationData.id,
          p_jurisdiction: jurisdiction,
          p_period: period,
          p_amount_collected_cents: line.amount,
        });
        if (accrueErr) {
          logger.error({ pi_id: pi.id, jurisdiction, period, err: accrueErr },
            'S17: tax_remittance_accrue failed — recoverable via reconciliation');
        }
      }
    }
  } else {
    logger.warn({ pi_id: pi.id, booking_id: bookingId },
      'S17: parent commission_split not found — tax breakdown not recorded');
  }
} else if (taxTotal > 0 && studioId) {
  // Single-line fallback: no breakdown but tax was charged — accrue under a default jurisdiction.
  // Use studio's location jurisdiction if available.
  const fallbackJurisdiction = 'UNKNOWN';                // Track C reconciliation will flag for re-categorization
  const eventDate = new Date();
  const quarter = Math.floor(eventDate.getMonth() / 3) + 1;
  const period = `${eventDate.getFullYear()}-Q${quarter}`;

  const fromUntypedSelect = supabase.from.bind(supabase) as unknown as (table: string) => {
    select: (cols: string) => {
      eq: (col: string, val: string) => {
        limit: (n: number) => {
          maybeSingle: () => Promise<{ data: { id: string } | null; error: unknown }>;
        };
      };
    };
  };
  const { data: locationData } = await fromUntypedSelect('locations')
    .select('id')
    .eq('studio_id', studioId)
    .limit(1)
    .maybeSingle();

  if (locationData) {
    await supabase.rpc(RPC.TAX_REMITTANCE_ACCRUE, {
      p_studio_id: studioId,
      p_location_id: locationData.id,
      p_jurisdiction: fallbackJurisdiction,
      p_period: period,
      p_amount_collected_cents: taxTotal,
    });
  }
}
```

Note: variable references like `studioId`, `bookingId` should already exist in scope from the prior commission_split_record block. If not, hoist them.

## Verification

1. `pnpm typecheck` zero new errors on `lib/payments/process-stripe-event.ts`.
2. `grep "RPC.COMMISSION_SPLIT_TAX_LINE_RECORD" lib/payments/process-stripe-event.ts` returns 1+ match.
3. `grep "RPC.TAX_REMITTANCE_ACCRUE" lib/payments/process-stripe-event.ts` returns 1+ match.
4. `grep "p_tax_amount_cents" lib/payments/process-stripe-event.ts` returns 1+ match.
5. `grep "amount_details" lib/payments/process-stripe-event.ts` returns 2+ matches (interface + reads).
6. No `any`. No `console.log`.

## Output

Report:
- File modified.
- Grep results.
- Tax mirror flow summary: PI succeeded → update charge tax → per-line accrue + commission split tax line → ledger entry per jurisdiction.
- Any deviation.

DO NOT TOUCH:
- `supabase/migrations/` (Track D owns)
- `workers/cron/` (Tracks B/C own)
- `lib/payments/contracts.ts` (just edited)
- Tests (Track E owns)
- `lib/stripe/charges.ts` (don't re-touch)

GO.

